course: dictionary
lesson: 8972
title: Sink: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so context tells you which one to use. «The stone sank» means it went down below the water. «Prices sank» means they fell lower in amount. The words around sink show you which meaning is right.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? A stone, a ship, the sun or a price can all sink, but each one means something a little different. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it.
explain: Sink can also be a noun, a basin with taps. «Wash your hands at the sink.» Phrases change the meaning too: «my heart sank» means you suddenly felt sad or worried.
fact: Sink (verb) means to go down below the top of water or another liquid, or to go down slowly.
fact: Sink (noun) means a basin with taps, found in a kitchen or bathroom.
fact: The forms are sink, sinks, sank, sunk and sinking.
fact: In science, an object sinks if it is denser than water, meaning heavy for its size, like a stone or a coin.
fact: «My heart sank» means I suddenly felt sad or worried; «sink or swim» means succeed or fail on your own.
exercise: «The sun sank behind the hills.» What does sank mean here? | To shine very brightly | To rise quickly into the sky | *To go down slowly | To wash clean
exercise: In a float or sink experiment, why does a stone sink? | It is too small to see | It is made of wood | *It is denser than water, so it is heavy for its size | It is lighter than the water
exercise: «Wash your hands at the sink.» What kind of word is sink here? | A verb, to go down | *A noun, a basin with taps | An adjective, describing wet hands | A number
test: «Prices sank last month.» What does sank mean? | To wash clean | To go to the bottom of the sea | To shine | *To fall lower in amount
test: In sport, what does it mean to sink a basket? | *To get the ball into the net | To sit down quietly | To run very fast | To tip over the basket
exam: «Hippos walk along the riverbed because their heavy bones make them sink.» What does sink mean here? | To sell at a lower price | To float up to the top | *To go down below the water | To wash clean
